# DAQiFi Core

.NET SDK + MCP tool for DAQiFi hardware. PublicAPI, CA2007, IDE0161, and the documented Git workflow (branch names, PRs against `main`) live in **CONTRIBUTING.md**. Never push `main`. Do not invent a commit-message dialect.

## TFMs

- Library, MCP tool, tests (`Daqifi.Core`, `Daqifi.Mcp`, `Daqifi.Core.Tests`, `Daqifi.Mcp.Tests`): `net9.0;net10.0`
- Benchmarks (`Daqifi.Core.Benchmarks`): `net10.0` only
- Not .NET 8. Do not multi-target the benchmark host.

## Layout — types that exist

```
src/Daqifi.Core/
  Device/                    IDevice, IStreamingDevice, DaqifiDevice, DaqifiStreamingDevice, ConnectionStatus
  Device/Discovery/          IDeviceFinder (not IDiscoveryService / DeviceDiscoveryService)
  Communication/Messages/    IOutboundMessage<T>, IInboundMessage<T>, ScpiMessage, ProtobufMessage
  Communication/Producers/   ScpiMessageProducer
  Communication/Consumers/   LineBasedMessageParser, ProtobufMessageParser
  Communication/Transport/   Tcp / Serial / Hid / Udp
  Channel/, Firmware/, Logging/
```

No `src/Daqifi.Core/Discovery/` and no `Connection/` tree. Connection lives on Device + Transport. Do not invent types.

## Messages

First-class parsers: SCPI (line-based) and protobuf. JSON is a device stream-format SCPI option (`ScpiMessageProducer.SetJsonStreamFormat`), not a library `IMessageParser`.

## ConnectionStatus

`Disconnected`, `Connecting`, `Connected`, `Lost`, `Retrying`, `Failed`.

## Build already owns this

- Nullable is on in `Directory.Build.props`. New files normally do not need `#nullable enable`; leave existing file-level directives unless a deliberate cleanup.
- New public API → `src/Daqifi.Core/PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt` (RS0016/RS0017). Intentional removal of shipped API → delete from `PublicAPI.Shipped.txt` + ApiCompat suppression. Do not send removals/renames only to Unshipped. Details: CONTRIBUTING.md.
- Awaits in `Daqifi.Core` → `ConfigureAwait(false)` (CA2007; tests exempt).
- File-scoped namespaces (IDE0161).
